  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Food Security and Livelihoods Response for returnees, IDPs and host communities in Renk.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CTP, through its partner ADA, is already implementing an emergency project with Sudan Appeal funding (ending on 31st May 2025) to respond to the acute crisis through WASH and FSL programming. Given the increasing numbers of returnees and refugees from Sudan and the escalating needs, the allocated GEF funding will cover the gaps in FSL programming. The aim is to establish a long-term CTP presence in Renk and seek further cash injections from other donors while maintaining some key WASH and FSL activities. 
With the current US funding freeze, many agencies are slowing or stopping their projects in Renk, and this has led to disruptions in food security and livelihoods. This project is anticipated to close some of the identified gaps in food security and livelihoods programming.</narrative>
  </description>
